Package: miraiWebR
Title: Parallel Tasks on Background webR Workers with a 'mirai'-Compatible API
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R: c(person("Lukas", "Widmer", email = "lukas_andreas.widmer@novartis.com",
                    role = c("aut", "cre")),
             person("Novartis", "Pharma AG", role = "cph"))
Author: Lukas Widmer [aut, cre],
  Novartis Pharma AG [cph]
Maintainer: Lukas Widmer <lukas_andreas.widmer@novartis.com>
Description: The 'mirai' package evaluates R expressions asynchronously in
    background R processes. WebAssembly R has no processes, sockets or threads, so
    'mirai' itself cannot run in webR. This package offers a subset of its interface
    -- daemons(), mirai(), mirai_map(), everywhere(), unresolved(), collect_mirai(),
    stop_mirai() and the m[] / m$data idioms -- on background webR sessions that the
    BAMDD with webR/brms/stanli application starts in Web Workers. Each worker is a
    complete R with the application's package library, so tasks run genuinely in
    parallel. A 'future' backend, plan(miraiWebR::webr_workers), makes the same
    workers available to future.apply, furrr and other 'future' clients.
    Features of 'mirai' without a webR counterpart stop with an error rather than
    being ignored.
